lisa-design:
- Compile is a method on *Env (limits and cache are per-Env, not global); cache keyed by (kind, source), RWMutex, no eviction (catalog-bounded).
- Whole-number float64/json.Number activation values are read as CEL ints (lazily, no tree copy), so state arithmetic like stackNext + 1 works on JSON-decoded numbers.
- Limits: cel.CostLimit plus a context timeout per evaluation; exceeding either is cel.limit (ErrCostLimit/ErrTimeout); a recover at the eval boundary turns panics into cel.eval errors.
- A literal string starting with = is written \=; a whole-string {{ params.x }} keeps the param's type (how dispatch.harness becomes an object); embedded placeholders accept scalars only; unknown params are ParamErrors.
- event.raw is not exposed to CEL (the contract keeps provider payloads away from rules); item.runs (from WorkItemView.RunsBySpec) backs item.lastRun.
- cel-go v0.31.0: v0.32 renamed the module to cel.dev/cel-go, which isn't the allow-listed path.

